LinkedIn News Asia shared a post: What would make you postpone retirement?

For SoftBank founder and CEO Masayoshi Son, it's AI. The 68-year-old says h=
e's shelving his retirement plans and intends to lead the company for anoth=
er 10 to 15 years as he pursues what he sees as the next phase of the AI re=
volution.=20

Dismissing concerns of an AI bubble, Son argued that the technology is stil=
l in its early stages. "The AI revolution has only just begun. For an indus=
try that is still at such an early stage, calling it a bubble is an insult,=
" he said.

Son isn't alone in working well beyond traditional retirement age. Warren B=
uffett remained CEO of Berkshire Hathaway until 94, while Oracle executive =
chairman Larry Ellison continues to play a major role in the company in his=
 80s.

What would motivate you to keep working beyond retirement age? Share your t=
houghts in the comments.

